{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fawning-dogtired-cutworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while authoring Cloud config-validation coverage for story 2127-348c-c41d-472e.\n\nThe DC transport rejects a non-https reconciler.base_url: ReconcilerConfig.__post_init__ (src/rebar/_config_schema.py) calls _validate_reconciler_tls, which raises ConfigError for any non-https scheme unless reconciler.allow_insecure is set. Cloud's JiraConfig (src/rebar/_config_schema.py, the jira.url/user/project dataclass) has NO __post_init__ and performs NO URL-scheme validation, so a cleartext http:// Jira URL is accepted silently — risking credential (PAT/basic-auth) exposure in transit.\n\nPinned as current behaviour by tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_config_validation.py::test_cloud_jira_config_does_not_reject_non_https_url_absence_documented (absence-documenting).\n\nAcceptance: JiraConfig rejects a non-https url with a ConfigError (mirroring _validate_reconciler_tls), with an allow_insecure-style override for trusted/loopback use; flip the absence-doc test to assert the rejection.","id":"bdb8-0646-9e13-4bfb","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud JiraConfig does not reject a non-https url (cleartext credential exposure)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785860371644742001,"uuid":"d2469c67-5af1-4f98-9f8a-9649b80cfda4"}